# KaraQueue settings. Copy this file to .env, fill in what you need, and leave the rest
# commented out: every line is optional and shows its default. The full list, with what each
# one does, is in docs/configuration.md. Paths below are inside the container from compose.yaml.

# --- Getting started ---------------------------------------------------------------------

# The admin page password. Leave it out and the server saves a one-time setup link to
# admin-setup-link.txt next to the database instead. Set at startup only.
# KARAQUEUE_ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# The address guests use, for the join link and QR code. Set it behind a reverse proxy.
# KARAQUEUE_PUBLIC_URL=https://karaoke.example.com

# Who can start rooms: "accounts" (an account or the admin password) or "anyone".
# KARAQUEUE_NEW_ROOMS=accounts

# Your reverse proxy's address or network, so rate limits see each guest's real address.
# Set at startup only.
# KARAQUEUE_TRUSTED_PROXIES=127.0.0.1

# --- Song library ------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Folders of karaoke videos, separated by ":". Turns on library search.
KARAQUEUE_MEDIA_DIR=/media
# Where songs saved from YouTube go for good. Empty means a YouTube folder in the first
# library folder; set it if the library is mounted read-only.
# KARAQUEUE_SAVE_DIR=
# "hosts" or "admins": who can save YouTube songs into the library.
# KARAQUEUE_WHO_SAVES=hosts
# KARAQUEUE_SAVES_PER_HOUR=10
# KARAQUEUE_SAVE_MAX_MB=500
# "musicbrainz" or "off": where Look up finds a song's real title and artist.
# KARAQUEUE_SONG_LOOKUP=musicbrainz
# Old-format videos (AVI, MPG...) converting at once, across every screen.
# KARAQUEUE_CONVERSIONS=2

# --- YouTube -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# A YouTube Data API key for search. Without one, search uses yt-dlp if downloads are on.
# KARAQUEUE_YOUTUBE_API_KEY=
# Turns on downloading YouTube songs to the server (the Docker image has yt-dlp and ffmpeg).
KARAQUEUE_DOWNLOADS_DIR=/data/downloads
# KARAQUEUE_DOWNLOADS_MAX_GB=10
# KARAQUEUE_DOWNLOADS_PER_HOUR=200
# The yt-dlp command, if it isn't on the PATH. Set at startup only.
# KARAQUEUE_YTDLP=yt-dlp
# A yt-dlp -f format string. The default picks mp4 up to 1080p.
# KARAQUEUE_YTDLP_FORMAT=

# --- Recordings --------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Turns on recording performances from a screen's mic.
KARAQUEUE_RECORDINGS_DIR=/data/recordings
# KARAQUEUE_RECORDING_MAX_MB=100
# KARAQUEUE_RECORDINGS_ROOM_MB=1000
# KARAQUEUE_RECORDINGS_MAX_GB=20

# --- Rooms and limits --------------------------------------------------------------------

# KARAQUEUE_SONGS_PER_SINGER=10
# KARAQUEUE_SINGERS_PER_ROOM=100
# KARAQUEUE_SCREENS_PER_ADDRESS=4
# KARAQUEUE_NAME_LIMIT=32
# KARAQUEUE_CODE_LENGTH=6
# 1 is normal, 2 doubles every cap, 0 turns rate limits off.
# KARAQUEUE_RATE_LIMIT=1
# Days before a room nobody has touched gets deleted. 0 keeps rooms forever.
# KARAQUEUE_ROOM_DAYS=30

# --- Public access -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# See docs/public-access.md. The easy way: a tunnel gives the server a public https address
# with nothing to set up on the router. "cloudflare" (no account), "cloudflare_named",
# "tailscale" or "off". The program has to be installed (the desktop app comes with cloudflared).
# KARAQUEUE_TUNNEL=off
# For "cloudflare_named": the token from the Cloudflare dashboard, and the hostname you gave it.
# KARAQUEUE_TUNNEL_TOKEN=
# KARAQUEUE_TUNNEL_HOSTNAME=karaoke.example.com
# The cloudflared and tailscale commands, if they aren't on the PATH. Set at startup only.
# KARAQUEUE_CLOUDFLARED=cloudflared
# KARAQUEUE_TAILSCALE=tailscale
# Or a free dynamic DNS name that follows your home connection:
# "duckdns", "noip", "dynu", "freedns", "custom" or "off".
# KARAQUEUE_DDNS_PROVIDER=off
# KARAQUEUE_DDNS_HOSTNAME=myparty.duckdns.org
# No-IP and Dynu only.
# KARAQUEUE_DDNS_USERNAME=
# The provider's token or password. Never shown on the admin page or written to the log.
# KARAQUEUE_DDNS_TOKEN=
# For "custom": the update address. {ip} and {hostname} get filled in.
# KARAQUEUE_DDNS_URL=
# KARAQUEUE_DDNS_MINUTES=5
# "on" asks the router to forward the port here (UPnP, NAT-PMP or PCP).
# KARAQUEUE_PORT_FORWARD=off
# The port on the router. 0 means the same as KARAQUEUE_FORWARD_TO_PORT. 443 makes the guest link https.
# KARAQUEUE_ROUTER_PORT=0
# The port on this machine the forward leads to. 0 means KARAQUEUE_PORT (plain http).
# Point it at an https server in front of KaraQueue, like Caddy on 443. Set in the environment only.
# KARAQUEUE_FORWARD_TO_PORT=0

# --- Server ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# These are set at startup only. The Docker image already sets the database path.
# KARAQUEUE_DB=/data/karaqueue.db
# KARAQUEUE_HOST=0.0.0.0
# KARAQUEUE_PORT=8000
# Folders the admin page may point the library, downloads and recordings at, separated by ":".
# KARAQUEUE_ALLOWED_FOLDERS=
